WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.816
This slide focuses on enumerate gives position and
value The goal is to understand

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:11.855
the idea in plain language before connecting it to
code or analytical use Loop

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:15.960
with a counter Sometimes you need both the item and
its position in the sequence

00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:22.417
Use a counter while looping Before running the
example predict

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:27.472
what the output should look like Run it in the
browser inspect the result then

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:33.249
change one value condition or input and run it again
Pay attention to what changed

00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:41.214
and why The number and customer are returned
together enumerate_loop.py

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.030
Control Flow & Decision Making
